<title>SWEDEN: POLL-Handelsbanken H1 profit seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-Handelsbanken H1 profit seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Handelsbanken's operating profit was expected to rise to 3.66 billion crowns in the first half of 1997 from 3.0 billion crowns a year ago, a Reuters poll of 12 analysts showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied between 3.32 and 4.08 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Credit losses were expected to more than halve to 428 million crowns from 952 million.</p>
<p>For the full year the operating profit was expected to rise to 7.45 billion crowns from 6.72 billion crowns in 1996.</p>
<p>Next year the bank's profit was expected to rise to 7.76 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aros, Carnegie, Den Norske Bank, Enskilda, C.I. Nordic Securities, Goldman Sachs, J.P. Morgan, James Capel, Morgan Stanley, Erik Penser, Swedbank, and Ohman.</p>
<p>Handelsbanken will release its half year report on August 19.</p>
